cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Thermal Image Calibration Tool: Empirical Line calibration of drone thermal images with field targets"
version: 0.3.0
date-released: 2026-11-24
authors:
  - family-names: Nelle
    given-names: Moritz
    affiliation: Haystack Imaging
license: GPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/haystack-imaging/thermal-calibration-tool"
url: "https://haystackimaging.eu"
keywords:
  - thermal imaging
  - UAV
  - drone
  - radiometric calibration
  - empirical line method
  - microbolometer drift
  - plant phenotyping
abstract: >-
  Desktop tool that corrects the drift and offset of uncooled thermal drone cameras using reference
  targets measured in the field. Fits the Empirical Line Method per calibration image, interpolates
  the correction over the flight, writes 32-bit float GeoTIFFs with their metadata, and reports the
  regression's prediction uncertainty per image.
